nt_uuid":"75a562f7-61fc-4865-9681-c8dda6d3fd48","position":{"commit_sha":"0942e332fffaa659ef502b207ee9dd677260a0ea","position":"1787946551386493001-75a562f7-61fc-4865-9681-c8dda6d3fd48"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"bf4ba7af8e6247696b6f07b1a1668ddf59c4bcdab8e585625cd5f1d606d869cd","event_uuid":"4037da8e-b539-43f8-8cbd-b5b70887576a","position":{"commit_sha":"84c0e6271f354c2a5348673047d2171fc10e53d2","position":"1787946560489184001-4037da8e-b539-43f8-8cbd-b5b70887576a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"4f7600a7325350f40d8d722d8f1620be496f615fe1e11476c0dc19ec26cf18a3","event_uuid":"0a0615c4-7ce6-45db-ac21-ec28447dff9d","position":{"commit_sha":"9614f0770faa789f6936d532eb3be8ec2f7b0c7a","position":"1787946564235228001-0a0615c4-7ce6-45db-ac21-ec28447dff9d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"plan_defect","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RCA (Phase 1 exit) — root cause PROVEN at runtime.\n\nMECHANISM: 9 sites derived the repo/config root as os.path.dirname(tracker). That equals the repo root ONLY for a co-located store. REBAR_TRACKER_DIR relocation is a SUPPORTED feature (deployed MCP server: store /var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets, code /app), where the tracker's parent has no rebar.toml, so every config read there resolves an EMPTY config.\n\nMOST SEVERE CONSEQUENCE (AC#1): transition_compute set repo_root_str = os.path.dirname(tracker) and fed it to gates.plan_review_precheck as the CONFIG root. On a relocated store the plan-review start-work-gate flag read from an empty config == OFF, so the 'transition open->in_progress' enforcement boundary SILENTLY STOPPED APPLYING.\n\nDISCRIMINATING EVIDENCE: reproduced OUTSIDE any tree containing a rebar.toml (an in-tree tmpdir masks the bug because _discover_project_config walks UP and finds the worktree's own rebar.toml). On a relocated store: 'claim' BLOCKS (already fixed by chuffy-arbored-goldfish) while 'transition open->in_progress' DID NOT block — the exact split predicted by the two code paths.\n\nATTRIBUTION: the AC#1 transition-gate escape was introduced by stab-bunch-foyer (65e3-1fc6-5f3b-4c67, commit 95577d196015, PR #49), which consolidated the shared start-work gate but wired the transition site's cfg_root to repo_root_str (= dirname(tracker)) while the claim side correctly used repo_root. chuffy-arbored-goldfish later fixed the claim path + gates.py signatures and explicitly deferred 'the rest' (these 9 sites) to THIS ticket, establishing the construct as a defect and REBAR_TRACKER_DIR relocation as a design invariant.\n\nLEGITIMACY: defect (behavior-preserving fix; co-located dirname(tracker) == git-toplevel == repo root). Standing intent unambiguous (prior Fixed: ticket chuffy-arbored-goldfish). Escalation rules checked -> PROCEED to fix; one design-laden site (run_sweep detached child) DEFERRED to a follow-up.","timestamp":1787939336936045001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"STEP 7 CLASS REVIEW + construct sweep.\n\nENUMERATED 9 SITES (this ticket's committed scope) — all addressed:\n- FIXED (8): _execute.py dispatcher (->None discover); transition.py:275 (->str(config.repo_root(repo_root)), fixes AC#1 gate + transitively close_ticket blame/scratch/compaction); transition.py:690 _unarchive; compact_trigger.py:107 ticket_needs_folding (threads repo_root) + :246 maybe_compact fallback (drops dirname); delete.py:390 scratch cleanup; validate.py:121 (config.repo_root_or_none()); _lib_gates.py:53 clarity threshold.\n- DEFERRED (1): compact_trigger.py:213 run_sweep (detached child, cwd IS the store; needs a spawn-contract change) -> follow-up scathing-custommade-bobcat (6bf1-326b-7404-4034), sanctioned '# repo-root-ok:' so the AC#4 guard passes with exactly one allowlisted site.\n\nBROADER CLASS FOUND (NOT in the enumerated 9) -> split to follow-up injurious-pugnacious-azurevase (c0f6-0fc9-fe48-41bc):\n- composer.py:274/:286 + composer_edit.py:141: cfg_root=os.path.dirname(str(tracker)) feeding description_cap_warning/duplicate_create_warning (compose_config + _plan_review_gate_applies). Same class, ADVISORY-only (never blocks a write). Clean but str()-wrapped, so the AC#4 guard (bare-form scope) does not catch it.\n- reads.py:238/:249/:374: dirname(realpath/abspath(tracker)) feeding compose_config sync.pull / tickets.branch / scratch.base_dir. NUANCED — these run 'git -C tracker_abs' on the STORE's OWN repo, so the tracker's parent may be the CORRECT root for sync/branch (AC#3's 'documents why' clause); resolving each needs a per-site design judgment, which is why it is split out rather than folded into this behavior-preserving change.\n\nKept THIS change to the committed 9 + the AC#4 guard (scoped to the bare os.path.dirname(tracker)/tracker_dir() form, exactly AC#4's wording) + RED->GREEN tests, mirroring the chuffy-arbored-goldfish scope-split discipline. The follow-up owns the str()/realpath()/abspath() variants AND the guard extension together.\n\nVALIDATION: RED->GREEN + mutation confirmed (restoring dirname(tracker) at transition.py:275 -> AC#1 DID NOT RAISE; at _lib_gates.py -> clarity threshold 5!=9). make lint + make typecheck green; 776 affected-area unit tests pass.","timestamp":1787939684425584001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787801685899463001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"9b5e7deb-d267-4458-8bec-455f60c58e93","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"8bb4-729e-6745-42d0"},{"link_uuid":"da7ffcbc-aa94-4714-8822-9dbebb8b70bd","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9c72-8c19-45b1-4bb6"},{"link_uuid":"fb996ecd-4dd8-4a3f-b7c8-4265935da8b0","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"220a-4581-0a64-43d6"},{"link_uuid":"ed53ca35-1a00-4a80-b96c-c501e1129a11","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"3c56-7748-dd3c-4aa2"},{"link_uuid":"0a0615c4-7ce6-45db-ac21-ec28447dff9d","provenance":"explicit","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"65e3-1fc6-5f3b-4c67"}],"description":"## Summary\n\n`os.path.dirname(tracker)` is used as a REPO/CONFIG root at **9 further sites** beyond the two\nfixed under `chuffy-arbored-goldfish`. That inference is correct only when the tracker sits\ninside the checkout. `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR` relocating the store is a supported feature\n(`_config_sources.tracker_dir_override`) and the deployed MCP server uses it — store at\n`/var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets`, repo at `/app` — so every one of these resolves a directory with\nno `rebar.toml`.\n\n## Sites (all verified present, `src/rebar`)\n\n- `_cli/_execute.py:86` — `fn(rest, tracker, os.path.dirname(tracker))`. The CLI dispatcher\n  passes this as `repo_root` to EVERY command, so the whole CLI inherits the assumption.\n- `_commands/transition.py:275` — `repo_root_str = os.path.dirname(tracker)`, then `:348`\n  feeds it to `gates.plan_review_precheck` — the OTHER start-work gate path, the sibling of\n  the claim site already fixed.\n- `_commands/transition.py:690` — `_unarchive(...)`\n- `_commands/compact_trigger.py:107` — `compose_config(os.path.dirname(tracker)).compact`\n- `_commands/compact_trigger.py:213`, `:246`\n- `_commands/delete.py:390` — `scratch.cleanup_for_ticket(...)`\n- `_engine_support/validate.py:121` — `repo_root=os.path.dirname(tracker)`\n- `_lib_gates.py:53` — `gates._clarity_threshold(os.path.dirname(tracker), None)`\n\n## Why this matters more than a wrong default\n\nProven under `chuffy-arbored-goldfish`: for a GATE FLAG, an empty config reads as OFF. The\nregression test there shows the plan-review start-work gate silently STOPS APPLYING on a\nrelocated store — `DID NOT RAISE` where it must block. `transition.py:275/:348` is the same\ngate reached through `transition open -> in_progress`, so the claim-side fix alone leaves that\ndoor open.\n\n## Scope note\n\n`chuffy-arbored-goldfish` deliberately fixed only the CLAIM path (`claim.py:116`, `:201`) plus\nthe `gates.py` signatures, keeping that change reviewable and inside its ticket's scope. This\nticket carries the rest. Split recorded with the operator's approval; the work is tracked here\nrather than dropped.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] `transition open -> in_progress` applies the plan-review gate on a relocated store.\n      (The claim-side equivalent is already pinned by\n      `test_plan_review_gate_still_applies_when_the_tracker_lives_outside_the_repo`.)\n- [x] The CLI dispatcher resolves a repo root that does not assume a co-located tracker.\n- [x] Each remaining site above resolves config from the repo root, or documents why the\n      tracker's parent is correct for it.\n- [x] A guard fails if a new `os.path.dirname(tracker)`-as-config-root site is introduced.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/transition.py","reason":"AC#1 primary fix: repo_root_str = str(config.repo_root(repo_root)); _unarchive root"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_execute.py","reason":"argv_tracker_root dispatcher passes None (discover) not dirname(tracker)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/delete.py","reason":"scratch.cleanup_for_ticket uses in-scope repo_root"},{"path":"src/rebar/_lib_gates.py","reason":"clarity threshold resolves from repo_root; removed local os import"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/compact_trigger.py","reason":"ticket_needs_folding threads repo_root; maybe_compact fallback drops dirname; run_sweep DEFERRED + sanctioned"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/validate.py","reason":"signature_findings resolves via config.repo_root_or_none() (ADR 0104 advisory)"},{"path":"scripts/check_repo_root_from_tracker.py","reason":"AC#4 guard: AST-flags dirname(<tracker>)-as-config-root; unparseable source reported loudly; sanction # repo-root-ok:"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_relocated_store_repo_root.py","reason":"RED->GREEN oracle: transition gate (AC#1), clarity threshold, delete scratch cleanup, config-off contrast"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_repo_root_from_tracker_guard.py","reason":"guard self-tests: both shapes, sanction, reasonless marker, unparseable source, make-lint wiring"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_cli_registry_dispatch.py","reason":"update dispatcher contract test: third arg now None (discover), was dirname(tracker)"},{"path":"Makefile","reason":"wire check_repo_root_from_tracker.py into make lint"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py","reason":"update argv_tracker_root adapter-contract comment: third arg now None (root discovered downstream)"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","220a-4581-0a64-43d6"],["relates_to","3c56-7748-dd3c-4aa2"],["relates_to","9c72-8c19-45b1-4bb6"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"75a562f7-61fc-4865-9681-c8dda6d3fd48","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"2ec7-be89-9b01-496a","ticket_type":"bug","title":"dirna